<title>FINLAND: UPM, Metsa-Serla up on deal.</title>
<headline>UPM, Metsa-Serla up on deal.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish forest industry groups UPM-Kymmene Oy and Metsa-Serla Oy rose in active trade on Tuesday following joint announcement of a units deal.</p>
<p>At 1220/1020 GMT, UPM traded at 98.00 markka, up four markka or over four percent. Turnover for UPM was lively at over 20 million markka.</p>
<p>Metsa-Serla was up 0.30 markka at 34.30.</p>
<p>UPM said on Tuesday it would in a series of deals sell two units to Metsa-Serla and pulp mill Metsa-Botnia.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom + 358 - 9 - 680 50 240</p>
</text>
